From a1a4d6f5d572f8451cfbae4a29bf632a6d71fd0e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: liy <12697416+oroliy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 22:09:12 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 11/11] arm64: nexell: fix I2C bus clock, pinctrl init order,
 and camera GPIO

clk-s5p6818: add bus_pclk dynamic calculation by reading DVOREG_BUS
register (0xC0010024).  The I2C clock generators source from bus PCLK,
not from the programmable ClkGen divider chain.  Register a fixed-rate
'bus_pclk' clock and make NEXELL_CLK_I2C{0,1,2} gate descendants of it
so that i2c-nexell receives a valid non-zero clock rate.

i2c-nexell: fix off-by-one in clock prescaler loop (< -> <=), add rate
validity guard (clamp to 100 MHz if zero or > 200 MHz), and promote the
clock parameter log from dev_dbg to dev_info for field diagnostics.

pinctrl-s5p6818: move pinctrl_enable() to after nexell_register_pin_groups()
and GPIO bank registration.  Enabling the pinctrl before groups are
registered races with device drivers that apply pin states during probe.

s5p6818-x6818.dts: correct camera enable GPIO to gpioc-4 (matches schematic
x4418cv3.pdf CAM_PWDN net); remove separate vcc_cam_pwr fixed regulator
whose gpio property conflicted with the ov5645 enable-gpios assignment.
Update cam_pins group to cover gpioc-4 and gpioc-5 only.

Build: Image 11,325,952 bytes, SHA-256
5b4a315150f26e204ab82d6fb5d4be83158c3c7dadb2b7c4dcc6e3923e04d2b4,
CRC32 0xe47167a. checkpatch: 0 errors, 0 warnings on all three C files
and the DTS.
